0.3976.50The claims recite a method and system that apply artificial intelligence, specifically a trained recurrent neural network (RNN), to process physiological data for predictive analysis, making them patent-eligible under 35 U.S.C. § 101. The claimed invention does not merely recite an abstract idea but instead integrates a machine-learning model into a technological process that transforms raw physiological signals into actionable insights for assessing fatigue in an athletic event. The claimed steps require a computing device to receive and transform electrical signals from biological sensors into physiological values such as heart rate and electrocardiogram (ECG) data, a process that inherently requires specialized data processing beyond human cognition. The invention further generates simulated animal data by modifying physiological and biomechanical parameters to predict conditions such as fatigue, which is not a mere mental process but a computationally intensive AI-driven simulation that enables forecasting of real-world conditions.
